<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kwahadi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Quahadi, Kwahadi Comanche</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kwahadi, or Antelope Eaters, were a division of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comanche">Comanche</a> who lived on the Llano Estacado of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> Panhandle. Among the last Plains peoples to resist the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, they fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-river-war">Red River War</a> of 1874–1875 under leaders including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quanah-parker">Quanah Parker</a>. Their surrender at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-sill">Fort Sill</a> in 1875 ended the independent Comanche presence on the southern Plains.</p></div>
